  "laneNotes": [
    "The Vermont family carries captions READ OUT OF THE PINNED BINARY rather than transcribed, and says so in its own field map. The trade is stated there: what a transcription adds is a second signal that the form changed, and the exact SHA-256 source binding already fails the family closed on any byte.",
    "200-00129 prints its signature block in a different order from the sealing form 200-00130 it otherwise matches: 42 is the street address, 39 the city and ZIP, 40 the phone and 41 the email. The finalizer caught the mismatch as explicit_mapping_conflicts_with_field_name rather than writing a phone number onto an address line.",
    "The Oregon family is STOPPED on one counter and its overlay directory does not exist. The reason is a measured anchor 34 points wide that cannot carry a telephone number at the minimum readable font; the row records exactly what would clear it.",
    "PF03 names the Oregon family's component assembly 'Oregon Marijuana Set-Aside Motion under ORS 475C.397'. That is a different route on a different form (OR-OJD-MJ-PCR). The track's recorded authority is ORS 137.225 and the assignment's own official forms are the ORS 137.225 packet and its Oregon State Police companion. The forms and the track agree; only the component label does not."
  ],
