      "whatStoppedIt": {
        "counter": "knownRequiredFieldsMissing",
        "count": 1,
        "field": "the participant's telephone number, on the measured Phone anchor of page 5 of the motion",
        "finalizerRefusal": "value_exceeds_widget_width_at_minimum_font",
        "detail": "Page 5 prints one rule under three labels -- Address, City, State, ZIP and Phone -- and the lane-C overlay profile splits that rule into three measured anchors of 174, 248 and 34 points. A telephone number does not fit in 34 points at the minimum readable font, so the flat overlay refused the anchor rather than clipping the value. A clipped telephone number on a filing is a wrong number, not a shorter one.",
        "whyNotRequiredBeforeFiling": "REQUIRED_BEFORE_FILING requires that the platform hold no value for the fact. It holds this one and writes it on other packets, so declaring it required-before-filing would be false and the contract says so in terms.",
        "whyTheFamilyIsStoppedRatherThanShipped": "Everything else in this packet is complete: eight anchors drawn, the route's Option 1 marked inside the box the court printed, 21 facts disclosed, the other eight counters zero. Returning it as built would have shipped a motion missing a contact number the platform holds.",
        "whatWouldClearIt": "Either a re-measurement of that rule that gives the Phone anchor the width the printed form actually leaves it, or a decision that the telephone number is not written on this document at all. Both are measurement or policy decisions, not build decisions, and neither is this lane's to make."
      },
